Let the cells be $c_{1}, c_{2}, \ldots, c_{4 m^{2}}$. Let $c_{i}$ be related to the set of cells $R_{i}$.  The number of cells in $R_{i}$ is $4 m - 1$.  We want to find the minimum number of blue cells such that for all $i$, $|R_{i} \cap \{ \text{blue cells} \}| \ge 2$.  Consider the sum $\sum_{i=1}^{4 m^{2}} |R_{i} \cap \{ \text{blue cells} \}|$.  This is the number of pairs of related cells where at least one of the cells is blue.  Since each cell is related to at least two blue cells, the sum is at least $2 \times 4 m^{2}$.  Each blue cell is related to $4 m - 1$ cells, so the sum is at most $(4 m - 1) \times (\text{number of blue cells})$.  Thus, the number of blue cells is at least $\frac{2 \times 4 m^{2}}{4 m - 1} = 2 m + \frac{2 m}{4 m - 1}$.  Since $m \ge 1$, $2 m + \frac{2 m}{4 m - 1}$ is greater than $2 m$.  Thus, we need at least $2 m + 1$ blue cells.

