The goat's position after $n$ moves is the sum of its position after $n-1$ moves and the vector describing its $n$th move. The length of this vector is $n$ and its direction is $90^{\circ}$ clockwise from the direction of the $(n-1)$th move.

If the goat's position after $n-1$ moves is $(x,y)$, then the vector describing its $n$th move is one of the following:
\begin{align*}
&\begin{pmatrix}n\\0\end{pmatrix} &\text{if }n-1\text{ is a multiple of }4,\\
&\begin{pmatrix}0\\-n\end{pmatrix} &\text{if }n-1\text{ is a multiple of }4+1,\\
&\begin{pmatrix}-n\\0\end{pmatrix} &\text{if }n-1\text{ is a multiple of }4+2,\\
&\begin{pmatrix}0\\n\end{pmatrix} &\text{if }n-1\text{ is a multiple of }4+3.
\end{align*}
This means that the goat's position after $n$ moves is one of the following:
\begin{align*}
&\begin{pmatrix}x+n\\y\end{pmatrix} &\text{if }n-1\text{ is a multiple of }4,\\
&\begin{pmatrix}x\\y-n\end{pmatrix} &\text{if }n-1\text{ is a multiple of }4+1,\\
&\begin{pmatrix}x-n\\y\end{pmatrix} &\text{if }n-1\text{ is a multiple of }4+2,\\
&\begin{pmatrix}x\\y+n\end{pmatrix} &\text{if }n-1\text{ is a multiple of }4+3.
\end{align*}

The goat has travelled a total of 55 units after 10 moves. The goat's position after 10 moves is
\begin{align*}
&\begin{pmatrix}0\\1\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}2\\0\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}0\\-3\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}-4\\0\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}0\\5\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}-6\\0\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}0\\7\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}-8\\0\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}0\\9\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}-10\\0\end{pmatrix}\\
&=\begin{pmatrix}-16\\16\end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
The goat's position after 11 moves is
\begin{align*}
&\begin{pmatrix}-16\\16\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}0\\-11\end{pmatrix}\\
&=\begin{pmatrix}-16\\5\end{pmatrix}.
\end{align*}
The goat's position after 12 moves is
\begin{align*}
&\begin{pmatrix}-16\\5\end{pmatrix}+\begin{pmatrix}-12\\0\end{pmatrix}\\
