question:
Determine all pairs of angles $(x, y)$ with $0^{\circ} \leq x<180^{\circ}$ and $0^{\circ} \leq y<180^{\circ}$ that satisfy the following system of equations:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\log _{2}(\sin x \cos y) & =-\frac{3}{2} \\
\log _{2}\left(\frac{\sin x}{\cos y}\right) & =\frac{1}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

response:
Taking the $\log_{10}$ of both sides of the given equation gives
\begin{align*}
\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right)^{\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right)} &= \log_{10}10000 \\
\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right)\cdot\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right) &= 4 \\
\left(\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right)\right)^2 &= 4
\end{align*}
Thus, $\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right)=2$ or $\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right)=-2$.

For the first case, we have
\begin{align*}
\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right) &= 2 \\
\log_{10}x &= 10^2 \\
x &= 10^{10^2} \\
x &= 10^{100}
\end{align*}
For the second case, we have
\begin{align*}
\log_{10}\left(\log_{10}x\right) &= -2 \\
\log_{10}x &= 10^{-2} \\
x &= 10^{10^{-2}} \\
x &= 10^{0.01}
\end{align*}
Thus, our solution set is $\boxed{10^{100}, 10^{0.01}}$.
</think>

<answer>\boxed{10^{100}, 10^{0.01}}</answer>

